# The stack's canonical tool declaration — the single source the verification
# surfaces derive from. `script/smoke` executes each tool row's proof over
# non-interactive ssh at runtime; test/declaration.sh holds the installers'
# smoke_gate calls to set equality with the tool rows; script/stack-docs
# generates the README inventory from all of it. Add one row per tool this
# stack ships, AND its `-- <proof>` group in scripts/{linux,darwin}/
# mise-install.sh — a row without its gate group, or a gate group without
# its row, fails `make test`. Ext rows are build-time membership claims; the
# first one also needs `<!-- extensions:begin/end -->` markers in README.md
# and a membership_gate call in both installers (stack-docs and the suite
# name each missing piece).
#
# tool|<name>|<binary>|<managed-by>|<proof>|<purpose>
#   name       canonical display name (== the mise key for plain mise: rows)
#   binary     what the proof executes (name, unless the validator's alias
#              table says otherwise)
#   managed-by mise:<key> | node-corepack | installer
#   proof      argv words, no shell syntax; `command -v <binary>` is the one
#              blessed existence form, pnpm/yarn rows only
# ext|<gate-token>|<source>   (only for stacks with a membership gate)
tool|node|node|mise:node|node --version|JS runtime baseline; replace or extend per the __STACK__ toolchain
tool|corepack|corepack|node-corepack|corepack --version|package-manager shim dispatcher, ships with Node 24 and earlier
tool|pnpm|pnpm|node-corepack|command -v pnpm|Corepack shim; resolves per-project via package.json packageManager
tool|yarn|yarn|node-corepack|command -v yarn|Corepack shim; resolves per-project via package.json packageManager
